'''Components Automobilístics de l'Istme, S.A.''' (CAI) is a Balboan automotive components manufacturer based in [[Sant Bart]]. The company produces replacement parts and components for both the domestic aftermarket and for {{w|completely knocked down|CKD}} assembly operations in the [[Portnou]]. It is listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] under the ticker CAU and is a constituent of the [[SCX 100]] index.

CAI was founded in 1992 by Francesc Maragall i Serra, a former engineer at [[Acereries de l'Istme]], who identified that the growing number of vehicles in Balboa — particularly in the used car market — was creating demand for domestic replacement parts manufacturing. The company initially produced brake components and suspension parts from domestically sourced steel, supplying the aftermarket for Volisanian and Okaiken vehicles that dominated the fleet at the time.

The company expanded into exhaust systems and wiring harnesses in the 2000s, and into {{w|electric vehicle battery|EV battery housings}} and electric drivetrain components in the 2010s, responding to the shift toward electric vehicle assembly in Portnou. CAI supplies components to both [[Yonezawa Balboa]] and [[Muntatge Automobilístic de Balboa|MAB]] for their CKD assembly operations, as well as to the domestic aftermarket.

Approximately 60 per cent of revenue is derived from aftermarket sales, with 25 per cent from CKD assembly supply contracts and 15 per cent from BTPMEU exports. The company sources steel from domestic producers including [[Acereries de l'Istme]] and [[Foneria General de Balboa]].

